                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I wish there was an conflicted mode for games like this.\n\nFrom a gameplay and artistic side of things.. it's a very enjoyable platforming experience. But from a technical side it lacks a lot of features.\n\nFull review video:\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WRW6-KFgewI&ab_channel=GuyLogic\n\nText:\nThe main issues i have with the title are a lack of online multiplayer (Local co-op just doesn't work that well on pc) and a severe lack of both mouse control, rebindable keys and graphical options. It's a VERY bare bones experience from a PC Tech perspective. \n\nI also experienced the rare, but noticeable, framedrops.\n\nFrom a gameplay side i feel the \"need\" to only use two keys really makes the experience much more simplified than it should be, and while it's quite fun as is... I feel it could be more so. Especially the jumping, sliding, interacting, wallgliding, mob-smashing leaves a bit to much to context of the environment, instead of control to the player.\n\nLastly, my issues is that each act has it's own \"player character\" and with little switching or variety to unlock they get boring...fast.\n\nAll in all a fun little indie experience, that leaves a few notable things to be desired. \n\n",
